    },
    "description": "🗃️ Real databases: rows, columns, cells, views, filters, sorts, relations. Find databases with search, inspect schema with get, query rows with query, then add_rows or set_cells. Reuse columnID and query rowID; sourceBlockID and cell value IDs are different. Never edit database cells through fs/block. Read action help for nested writes.
Actions (required fields): get(avID) · query(avID) · create(parentID) · update_view*(avID, blockID, viewID) · search(keyword) · add_rows(avID) · remove_rows(avID) · add_column(avID, keyName, keyType) · remove_column(avID) · rename(avID) · set_cells(avID) · set_column_options*(avID, keyID, options) · duplicate_rows*(avID, sourceRowIDs) · duplicate(avID) · add_view(avID, blockID, viewID, layout, name) · set_new_item_templates*(avID, blockID, templates, defaultTemplateID) · create_from_template*(avID, blockID, templateID) · configure_two_way_relation*(avID, blockID, keyID, destinationAvID, backRelationKeyID, sourceName, destinationName) · configure_rollup*(avID, blockID, keyID, relationKeyID, destinationKeyID, calc) · set_relation*(avID, blockID, itemID, keyID, relatedItemIDs)
* = ask the user to confirm first. action="help" (topic=<action>) returns optional fields, nested shapes, and examples.",
    "overview": {
      "actionSummaries": {
        "add_column": "Use avID + keyName + keyType, and optionally keyID or blockID. MCP generates keyID automatically when omitted. Supported keyType values match the 16 SiYuan addable column types, including keyType="mSelect", keyType="mAsset", and keyType="lineNumber". Optional blockID must be a registered database block for this AV if you need to pin a specific block view.",
        "add_rows": "Rows without cells: use avID + blockIDs for bound rows, or avID + primaryKeyTexts for detached rows. Composite mode: use avID + rows:[{clientKey, primaryKeyText, cells:[{columnID, valueType, ...}]}], mutually exclusive with blockIDs/primaryKeyTexts. Composite rows are preflighted as one batch, receive stable rowIDs before any write, then write initial cells in a second native phase. MCP checkpoints reserved → rows_created → cells_written → verified. A failure after rows exist returns exact rowIDs and a stage; never re-run add_rows for those rows. Cells use the same typed fields as set_cells (e.g. {columnID,valueType:"number",number:9}); see av(action="help", topic="set_cells") for the full valueType table.",
        "add_view": "Provide avID + exact NodeAttributeView blockID + a new stable viewID + table/gallery/kanban + name. First run validateOnly=true. It does not use render; kanban requires an existing select key to avoid an implicit schema write.",
        "configure_rollup": "Dangerous schema operation for an existing rollup key. Pass its existing relation key, destination key, and the native RollupCalc object exactly as SiYuan defines it. MCP does not invent calculation aliases. SiYuan may remove filters that reference the reconfigured rollup key.",
        "configure_two_way_relation": "Dangerous schema operation for an existing relation key. Pass source and destination AV identities plus a stable reverse-key ID. MCP verifies both writable database carriers, uses the native updateAttrViewColRelation transaction, and reads both directions back. It refuses to retarget an existing relation that would mutate an unpreflighted third AV.",
        "create": "Use parentID (an existing document or block) and optionally a new avID; preflight first. A new database starts unnamed with a primary key column (type block) and one select column; use rename to set the database and column names and remove_column to drop the select column. Same requestId replays saved IDs, stages and original result before checking existence. Unknown or partial creation must not be retried with another ID.",
        "create_from_template": "Dangerous native creation using an existing template. itemID in the result is the AV row identity; blockID is the separate bound block/document identity. MCP preflights all default fields and relation targets, then reads every requested default back. Document templates require an explicit saveLocation so the target notebook can be authorized; inherited global document location is intentionally not guessed.",
        "duplicate": "Matches SiYuan copy-as-mirror behavior: call the kernel duplicate API, spin the AV block DOM, then commit an insert transaction. previousID overrides the insertion target; otherwise MCP uses blockID or the resolved owning database block.",
        "duplicate_rows": "Dangerous: use avID + ordered sourceRowIDs for bound, persistent top-level row items only; each becomes a detached text record. First call validateOnly=true, then confirm and submit expectedManifestHash + requestId. MCP checks every resolved two-way-relation destination AV carrier for rw/rwd before dispatch and verifies source placement plus reverse links after a normal response. Never retry automatically after outcome_unknown.",
        "get": "Use avID with scope=structure (default), columns, view, or raw. structure never contains row IDs or values. Optional blockID proves database context; viewID selects reading only. Use query for records.",
        "query": "Use avID, optional keyword/page/pageSize/fields, and mode=rows (default) or primary_keys. fields is a list of stable columnIDs: requested cells and columns are returned and rowID is always kept. Row mode supports viewID/blockID/groupPaging. Primary-key mode rejects viewID/groupPaging/fields and defaults to 16 rows. Follow nextSteps only when present.",
        "remove_column": "Use avID + keyID, and optionally blockID to target a specific registered database block. removeRelationDest only matters for relation columns.",
        "remove_rows": "Use avID + rowIDs (canonical AV row item IDs) to remove rows after the server validates every identity against the current AV. srcIDs remains the explicitly native interface and is not an interchangeable alias; mixing rowIDs and srcIDs is rejected before any write. Optional blockID pins a specific registered database block when you need explicit block-view context.",
        "rename": "Use avID + name to rename the database, and/or keyID + keyName to rename one column, including the primary key column that av(action="create") names by default. Types and values are unchanged. Get key IDs from av(action="get"). Strict write: preflight with validateOnly=true, then commit with the returned requestId and expectedStateHash.",
        "search": "Searches AV/database definitions by keyword and post-filters unreadable results. Unresolvable matches remain discoverable in unresolvedResults, alongside raw result counts and filtering reasons. Match scope primarily covers AV names plus primary-key fallback results, not arbitrary cell text.",
        "set_cells": "Use avID + cells[]. Each item requires rowID + columnID + valueType and its matching typed field. For a single-cell write, pass rowID + columnID + valueType directly. rowID must be the AV row item ID stored in value.blockID, not value.id or the bound source block ID. Optional blockID must be a registered database block for this AV if you need to pin a specific block view. valueType="mAsset" accepts assets[]. Relation values are intentionally rejected here; use set_relation so MCP can authorize the destination AV and read back the reverse cell. Cell fields by valueType: text→text:"…"; number→number:9; date→date:"2026-01-31" or epoch ms; checkbox→checked:true; select→option:"在读"; multi_select (column type mSelect)→options:["a","b"]; url/email/phone→url/email/phone:"…"; relation→relationBlockIDs:[…]; mAsset→assets:[{type,content}]. Example: {rowID,columnID,valueType:"select",option:"在读"}.",
        "set_column_options": "Dangerous: use avID + keyID + the complete options array for a select or mSelect key. This is a replacement, not a patch: omitted names are removed. First call the same action with validateOnly=true; after confirmation submit the returned expectedStateHash and the returned requestId. If new names are observed in SiYuan append order, MCP reports intermediate_option_order and requires a new preflight before any explicit reorder.",
        "set_new_item_templates": "Dangerous complete replacement of ordered native new-item templates. Pass every template and defaultTemplateID, not a patch. MCP captures a canonical complete-template preimage, validates each key and select/mSelect option against the raw AV, performs one native transaction, and verifies order, default, and all remaining template fields through getAttributeView. Missing options are rejected rather than added or silently pruned.",
        "set_relation": "Dangerous complete replacement of one relation cell. blockID is the verified source database carrier; itemID and relatedItemIDs are AV row item IDs, never bound document block IDs. An empty relatedItemIDs array clears the relation. MCP authorizes destination writes and verifies source plus two-way reverse cells without retrying an unknown response.",
        "update_view": "Use avID + blockID + current viewID and at least one of filters, sorts, group, columnVisibility:[{columnID,hidden}], columnOrder:[columnID]. Arrays replace except visibility, which changes listed columns only. Empty visibility alone is rejected. Filter nodes must not mix group fields (combination/filters) with leaf fields (column/operator/value); groups contain only combination and filters. Preflight validates all configurations before one transaction; readback protects every unrequested property.",
      },
      "actions": {
        "add_column": {
          "hint": "Use avID + keyName + keyType, and optionally keyID or blockID. MCP generates keyID automatically when omitted. Supported keyType values match the 16 SiYuan addable column types, including keyType="mSelect", keyType="mAsset", and keyType="lineNumber". Optional blockID must be a registered database block for this AV if you need to pin a specific block view.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "add_rows": {
          "hint": "Rows without cells: use avID + blockIDs for bound rows, or avID + primaryKeyTexts for detached rows. Composite mode: use avID + rows:[{clientKey, primaryKeyText, cells:[{columnID, valueType, ...}]}], mutually exclusive with blockIDs/primaryKeyTexts. Composite rows are preflighted as one batch, receive stable rowIDs before any write, then write initial cells in a second native phase. MCP checkpoints reserved → rows_created → cells_written → verified. A failure after rows exist returns exact rowIDs and a stage; never re-run add_rows for those rows. Cells use the same typed fields as set_cells (e.g. {columnID,valueType:"number",number:9}); see av(action="help", topic="set_cells") for the full valueType table.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "add_view": {
          "hint": "Provide avID + exact NodeAttributeView blockID + a new stable viewID + table/gallery/kanban + name. First run validateOnly=true. It does not use render; kanban requires an existing select key to avoid an implicit schema write.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "configure_rollup": {
          "hint": "Dangerous schema operation for an existing rollup key. Pass its existing relation key, destination key, and the native RollupCalc object exactly as SiYuan defines it. MCP does not invent calculation aliases. SiYuan may remove filters that reference the reconfigured rollup key.",
          "requiresConfirmation": true,
        },
        "configure_two_way_relation": {
          "hint": "Dangerous schema operation for an existing relation key. Pass source and destination AV identities plus a stable reverse-key ID. MCP verifies both writable database carriers, uses the native updateAttrViewColRelation transaction, and reads both directions back. It refuses to retarget an existing relation that would mutate an unpreflighted third AV.",
          "requiresConfirmation": true,
        },
        "create": {
          "hint": "Use parentID (an existing document or block) and optionally a new avID; preflight first. A new database starts unnamed with a primary key column (type block) and one select column; use rename to set the database and column names and remove_column to drop the select column. Same requestId replays saved IDs, stages and original result before checking existence. Unknown or partial creation must not be retried with another ID.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "create_from_template": {
          "hint": "Dangerous native creation using an existing template. itemID in the result is the AV row identity; blockID is the separate bound block/document identity. MCP preflights all default fields and relation targets, then reads every requested default back. Document templates require an explicit saveLocation so the target notebook can be authorized; inherited global document location is intentionally not guessed.",
          "requiresConfirmation": true,
        },
        "duplicate": {
          "hint": "Matches SiYuan copy-as-mirror behavior: call the kernel duplicate API, spin the AV block DOM, then commit an insert transaction. previousID overrides the insertion target; otherwise MCP uses blockID or the resolved owning database block.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "duplicate_rows": {
          "hint": "Dangerous: use avID + ordered sourceRowIDs for bound, persistent top-level row items only; each becomes a detached text record. First call validateOnly=true, then confirm and submit expectedManifestHash + requestId. MCP checks every resolved two-way-relation destination AV carrier for rw/rwd before dispatch and verifies source placement plus reverse links after a normal response. Never retry automatically after outcome_unknown.",
          "requiresConfirmation": true,
        },
        "get": {
          "hint": "Use avID with scope=structure (default), columns, view, or raw. structure never contains row IDs or values. Optional blockID proves database context; viewID selects reading only. Use query for records.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "query": {
          "hint": "Use avID, optional keyword/page/pageSize/fields, and mode=rows (default) or primary_keys. fields is a list of stable columnIDs: requested cells and columns are returned and rowID is always kept. Row mode supports viewID/blockID/groupPaging. Primary-key mode rejects viewID/groupPaging/fields and defaults to 16 rows. Follow nextSteps only when present.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "remove_column": {
          "hint": "Use avID + keyID, and optionally blockID to target a specific registered database block. removeRelationDest only matters for relation columns.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "remove_rows": {
          "hint": "Use avID + rowIDs (canonical AV row item IDs) to remove rows after the server validates every identity against the current AV. srcIDs remains the explicitly native interface and is not an interchangeable alias; mixing rowIDs and srcIDs is rejected before any write. Optional blockID pins a specific registered database block when you need explicit block-view context.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "rename": {
          "hint": "Use avID + name to rename the database, and/or keyID + keyName to rename one column, including the primary key column that av(action="create") names by default. Types and values are unchanged. Get key IDs from av(action="get"). Strict write: preflight with validateOnly=true, then commit with the returned requestId and expectedStateHash.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "search": {
          "hint": "Searches AV/database definitions by keyword and post-filters unreadable results. Unresolvable matches remain discoverable in unresolvedResults, alongside raw result counts and filtering reasons. Match scope primarily covers AV names plus primary-key fallback results, not arbitrary cell text.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "set_cells": {
          "hint": "Use avID + cells[]. Each item requires rowID + columnID + valueType and its matching typed field. For a single-cell write, pass rowID + columnID + valueType directly. rowID must be the AV row item ID stored in value.blockID, not value.id or the bound source block ID. Optional blockID must be a registered database block for this AV if you need to pin a specific block view. valueType="mAsset" accepts assets[]. Relation values are intentionally rejected here; use set_relation so MCP can authorize the destination AV and read back the reverse cell. Cell fields by valueType: text→text:"…"; number→number:9; date→date:"2026-01-31" or epoch ms; checkbox→checked:true; select→option:"在读"; multi_select (column type mSelect)→options:["a","b"]; url/email/phone→url/email/phone:"…"; relation→relationBlockIDs:[…]; mAsset→assets:[{type,content}]. Example: {rowID,columnID,valueType:"select",option:"在读"}.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "set_column_options": {
          "hint": "Dangerous: use avID + keyID + the complete options array for a select or mSelect key. This is a replacement, not a patch: omitted names are removed. First call the same action with validateOnly=true; after confirmation submit the returned expectedStateHash and the returned requestId. If new names are observed in SiYuan append order, MCP reports intermediate_option_order and requires a new preflight before any explicit reorder.",
          "requiresConfirmation": true,
        },
        "set_new_item_templates": {
          "hint": "Dangerous complete replacement of ordered native new-item templates. Pass every template and defaultTemplateID, not a patch. MCP captures a canonical complete-template preimage, validates each key and select/mSelect option against the raw AV, performs one native transaction, and verifies order, default, and all remaining template fields through getAttributeView. Missing options are rejected rather than added or silently pruned.",
          "requiresConfirmation": true,
        },
        "set_relation": {
          "hint": "Dangerous complete replacement of one relation cell. blockID is the verified source database carrier; itemID and relatedItemIDs are AV row item IDs, never bound document block IDs. An empty relatedItemIDs array clears the relation. MCP authorizes destination writes and verifies source plus two-way reverse cells without retrying an unknown response.",
          "requiresConfirmation": true,
        },
        "update_view": {
          "hint": "Use avID + blockID + current viewID and at least one of filters, sorts, group, columnVisibility:[{columnID,hidden}], columnOrder:[columnID]. Arrays replace except visibility, which changes listed columns only. Empty visibility alone is rejected. Filter nodes must not mix group fields (combination/filters) with leaf fields (column/operator/value); groups contain only combination and filters. Preflight validates all configurations before one transaction; readback protects every unrequested property.",
          "requiresConfirmation": true,
        },
      },
      "advancedActions": [
        "add_rows",
        "remove_rows",
        "add_column",
        "remove_column",
        "rename",
        "set_cells",
        "set_column_options",
        "duplicate_rows",
        "duplicate",
        "add_view",
        "update_view",
        "set_new_item_templates",
        "create_from_template",
        "configure_two_way_relation",
        "configure_rollup",
