  "document": {
    "actions": {
      "create": {
        "action": "create",
        "example": {
          "action": "create",
          "markdown": "正文从这里开始，不要再写 # New Child。",
          "notebook": "20210808180117-czj9bvb",
          "path": "/Folder/Parent/New Child",
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "description": "The path is inside the notebook. Do not include the notebook name, and do not pass a .sy storage path here.",
            "mcp": {
              "action": "create",
              "markdown": "正文从这里开始，不要再写 # New Child。",
              "notebook": "20210808180117-czj9bvb",
              "path": "/Folder/Parent/New Child",
            },
            "title": "Create a child document by notebook-local hpath (recommended)",
          },
          {
            "description": "Use this when the parent hpath is already known and you want the title separated from the parent path.",
            "mcp": {
              "action": "create",
              "markdown": "正文从这里开始，不要再写 # New Child。",
              "notebook": "20210808180117-czj9bvb",
              "parentPath": "/Folder/Parent",
              "title": "New Child",
            },
            "title": "Create with a human-readable parent hpath plus title",
          },
          {
            "description": "Only parentPath accepts this .sy storage path form; path does not.",
            "mcp": {
              "action": "create",
              "notebook": "20210808180117-czj9bvb",
              "parentPath": "/20240318112233-abc123.sy",
              "title": "New Child",
            },
            "title": "Create with a storage parent path returned by lookup",
          },
        ],
        "fullDocResource": "siyuan://help/action/document/create",
        "guidance": [
          "For ordinary document file operations, prefer fs(action="ls"|"tree"|"read"|"write"|"search") because it accepts human-readable paths and hides storage paths and IDs.",
          "document(action="create") creates both non-empty and empty documents. Prefer path for child documents; path is a notebook-local human-readable hpath such as /Folder/Parent/New Child, not /Notebook/Folder/... and not a .sy storage path.",
          "Do not put # Title at the start of document(action="create") markdown. SiYuan renders the document title as H1 automatically, and MCP strips a matching leading H1 to avoid duplicate titles.",
          "document(action="create", parentPath=..., title=...) is also supported. parentPath accepts either a notebook-local human-readable parent hpath such as /Folder/Parent, or a storage path ending in .sy returned by document(action="lookup").",
          "fs(action="write", path="/Notebook/Folder/Doc") uses a workspace path and should include the notebook name for unambiguous resolution; omission works only for a unique existing document or parent. document(action="create", notebook=..., path="/Folder/Doc") uses a notebook-local hpath and must omit the notebook name. Do not mix these two path formats.",
          "If document(action="create") reports a duplicate-name error, verify the intended child with document(action="lookup", notebook=..., hpath="/Folder/Parent/New Child", include=["id","path","hpath"]) or document(action="get_child_docs", id=<parent-doc-id>). New create results may take a short indexing delay before lookup/search sees them.",
          "document(action="ensure_link_targets") is the bounded import-link provisioner: scope it with notebook + parentId, reuse only explicit child document IDs, and use create only for explicit new titles. It never guesses an existing target from a title; same-title children are unresolved and require an ID decision.",
          "For recently created documents, document(action="lookup", hpath=...) may briefly lag behind create because it depends on SiYuan indexing; retry if needed.",
          "document(action="lookup", id=...) may hit the same short indexing delay right after create; MCP retries briefly and then returns a timing-specific hint if indexing still has not settled.",
        ],
        "hint": "Use a notebook ID from notebook.list, never its name. Use notebook + path for the most direct child-document flow. path is a notebook-local hpath like /Folder/Parent/New Child, not /Notebook/... and not .sy. parentPath + title is also supported. markdown is optional and must not start with # Title; a matching leading H1 is stripped to avoid duplicate titles.",
        "parameters": {
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "description": "Create a new document. notebook is an ID from notebook.list, never a notebook name. Requires notebook + path OR notebook + parentPath + title in every mode; notebook + title alone is invalid. Use parentPath=/ for the notebook root. Prefer path for child documents; parentPath + title also accepts a human-readable parent path or a storage path ending in .sy.",
          "oneOf": [
            {
              "not": {
                "anyOf": [
                  {
                    "required": [
                      "parentPath",
                    ],
                  },
                  {
                    "required": [
                      "title",
                    ],
                  },
                ],
              },
              "required": [
                "path",
              ],
            },
            {
              "not": {
                "required": [
                  "path",
                ],
              },
              "required": [
                "parentPath",
                "title",
              ],
            },
          ],
          "properties": {
            "action": {
              "const": "create",
              "type": "string",
            },
            "icon": {
              "description": "Optional document icon. Prefer a Unicode hex code string such as '1f4d4' for 📔 instead of a raw emoji character.",
              "type": "string",
            },
            "markdown": {
              "description": "Markdown content, defaults to empty. Do not include a leading # Title; a matching H1 is stripped automatically.",
              "type": "string",
            },
            "notebook": {
              "description": "Notebook ID",
              "type": "string",
            },
            "parentPath": {
              "description": "Parent path for title-based creation, relative to the notebook root. Accepts a human-readable path (must start with /, MUST NOT include the notebook name) or a storage path ending in .sy returned by document(action="lookup").",
              "type": "string",
            },
            "path": {
              "description": "Human-readable target path, relative to the notebook root. Must start with / and MUST NOT include the notebook name (e.g., /Folder/Doc, not /NotebookName/Folder/Doc). Parent paths must already exist.",
              "type": "string",
            },
            "sorts": {
              "description": "Compatibility option retained for older callers; title-based creation now uses the reliable path flow",
              "items": {
                "type": "string",
              },
              "type": "array",
            },
            "title": {
              "description": "Required together with parentPath when create omits path; notebook + title alone is invalid",
              "type": "string",
            },
          },
          "required": [
            "action",
            "notebook",
          ],
          "type": "object",
        },
        "requiredFields": [
          [
            "notebook",
            "path",
          ],
          [
            "notebook",
            "parentPath",
            "title",
          ],
        ],
        "requiresConfirmation": false,
        "shapes": [
          "notebook + path",
          "notebook + parentPath + title",
        ],
        "tool": "document",
        "writeWorkflow": [
          "Confirm the user-authorized target and operation scope.",
          "Call the same action with validateOnly=true to obtain preflight.commitArgs.",
          "Read the returned preview (targets, changes, risk) and confirm it matches the intended change; if not, do not commit. preview="full" returns complete before/after text.",
          "Copy preflight.commitArgs unchanged as the next call arguments; do not edit requestId, hashes, or business fields.",
          "Read the target back or inspect the returned receipt before reporting success.",
        ],
      },
