    },
    "description": "🔍 Workspace content discovery: fulltext for keywords/syntax/regex, semantic for meaning, query_sql for SELECT queries (add LIMIT; table blocks), backlinks and refs. Use fs.search for Markdown lines under a known path, document.search_docs for titles, av.search for database names. Read matched content before editing; find_replace is the only write.
Actions (required fields): fulltext(query) · semantic(query) · query_sql() · get_backlinks(id) · search_refs(id) · find_replace*(k, r, ids) · search_assets() · fulltext_asset_content() · list_invalid_refs()
* = ask the user to confirm first. action="help" (topic=<action>) returns optional fields, nested shapes, and examples.",
    "overview": {
      "actionSummaries": {
        "find_replace": "This is the mutating exception inside the search tool. It performs content replacement after write-permission checks and still requires explicit user confirmation.",
        "fulltext": "Pass a query string. Supports keyword, query syntax, SQL, and regex modes via methodName (preferred) or method. fulltext now returns plainContent/excerpt by default. types accepts shortcodes directly: {"h": true, "c": true} auto-expands to {"heading": true, "codeBlock": true}. Use sortBy="relevance" or "date" instead of numeric orderBy. Use parentId to scope within a document, hasTags to filter tagged blocks.",
        "fulltext_asset_content": "Searches indexed asset/OCR text. Prefer methodName and sortBy over numeric method/orderBy. Provide assetId for an exact asset-content lookup.",
        "get_backlinks": "Returns documents that contain references and/or text mentions for the given block ID (backlinks/backmentions, grouped by document), plus refBlocks: the exact blocks that reference it, with their content (same rows as search_refs). Use mode="links" | "mentions" | "both". Partial permission-filtered results include machine-readable metadata.",
        "list_invalid_refs": "no extra fields",
        "query_sql": "Execute a SELECT statement. Common tables: blocks, spans, assets. Prefer sql over stmt when prompting an AI. Always use LIMIT to control result size. User-selected columns are preserved. Raw SQL and fulltext SQL mode are rejected while any notebook is unreadable because arbitrary SQL cannot be safely post-filtered by notebook. Use document(action="query") for permission-scoped document lists and statistics.",
        "search_assets": "Searches asset filenames. Prefer query over k when prompting an AI. If you need OCR or indexed inner-text matches, use fulltext_asset_content instead.",
        "search_refs": "Returns the blocks whose content references the target id (block refs to that block or document), each with its own content and ref_text. Empty when nothing references id. Use rootID to limit to one referencing document and k to filter by keyword; get_backlinks groups by document and can include unlinked mentions.",
        "semantic": "Searches SiYuan’s native embedding index by meaning. Requires SiYuan 3.7.0+ and an enabled, indexed embedding model. Supports paths, types/typeShortcodes, subTypes, page, and pageSize; encrypted notebooks are not included in the native embedding index.",
      },
      "actions": {
        "find_replace": {
          "hint": "This is the mutating exception inside the search tool. It performs content replacement after write-permission checks and still requires explicit user confirmation.",
          "requiresConfirmation": true,
        },
        "fulltext": {
          "hint": "Pass a query string. Supports keyword, query syntax, SQL, and regex modes via methodName (preferred) or method. fulltext now returns plainContent/excerpt by default. types accepts shortcodes directly: {"h": true, "c": true} auto-expands to {"heading": true, "codeBlock": true}. Use sortBy="relevance" or "date" instead of numeric orderBy. Use parentId to scope within a document, hasTags to filter tagged blocks.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "fulltext_asset_content": {
          "hint": "Searches indexed asset/OCR text. Prefer methodName and sortBy over numeric method/orderBy. Provide assetId for an exact asset-content lookup.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "get_backlinks": {
          "hint": "Returns documents that contain references and/or text mentions for the given block ID (backlinks/backmentions, grouped by document), plus refBlocks: the exact blocks that reference it, with their content (same rows as search_refs). Use mode="links" | "mentions" | "both". Partial permission-filtered results include machine-readable metadata.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "list_invalid_refs": {
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "query_sql": {
          "hint": "Execute a SELECT statement. Common tables: blocks, spans, assets. Prefer sql over stmt when prompting an AI. Always use LIMIT to control result size. User-selected columns are preserved. Raw SQL and fulltext SQL mode are rejected while any notebook is unreadable because arbitrary SQL cannot be safely post-filtered by notebook. Use document(action="query") for permission-scoped document lists and statistics.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "search_assets": {
          "hint": "Searches asset filenames. Prefer query over k when prompting an AI. If you need OCR or indexed inner-text matches, use fulltext_asset_content instead.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "search_refs": {
          "hint": "Returns the blocks whose content references the target id (block refs to that block or document), each with its own content and ref_text. Empty when nothing references id. Use rootID to limit to one referencing document and k to filter by keyword; get_backlinks groups by document and can include unlinked mentions.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "semantic": {
          "hint": "Searches SiYuan’s native embedding index by meaning. Requires SiYuan 3.7.0+ and an enabled, indexed embedding model. Supports paths, types/typeShortcodes, subTypes, page, and pageSize; encrypted notebooks are not included in the native embedding index.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
      },
      "advancedActions": [
        "search_refs",
        "find_replace",
        "search_assets",
        "fulltext_asset_content",
        "list_invalid_refs",
      ],
      "commonActions": [
        "fulltext",
        "semantic",
        "query_sql",
        "get_backlinks",
      ],
      "detailsHint": "Call search(action="help", topic="<actionName>") for required fields, shapes, and a minimal example.",
      "guidance": [
        "For permission-scoped document inventories, body statistics, and same-title candidates, use document(action="query"). SQL mode in fulltext has the same all-notebooks-readable requirement as query_sql.",
        "All search actions are read-only except find_replace, which modifies content and requires explicit user confirmation.",
        "search(action="query_sql") only accepts SELECT statements and preserves user-selected columns. Raw SQL is available only when every notebook is readable because aggregate, join, CTE, and subquery results cannot be safely post-filtered by notebook.",
        "When calling query_sql, always add LIMIT yourself. MCP may still truncate large result sets and will tell you when to refine the query.",
        "The blocks table columns include: id, parent_id, root_id, box, path, hpath, name, alias, memo, tag, content, fcontent, markdown, length, type, subtype, ial, sort, created, updated.",
        "In SQL results, blocks.type uses SiYuan short codes such as d=document, h=heading, p=paragraph, l=list, i=list-item, b=blockquote, c=code, m=math, t=table, html=html, video=video, audio=audio, widget=widget.",
        "Use search(action="fulltext") for exact keyword or syntax searches, search(action="semantic") for meaning-based discovery, and search(action="query_sql") for structured queries.",
        "search(action="fulltext") types field auto-expands shortcodes: {"h": true, "p": true} is equivalent to {"heading": true, "paragraph": true}. Shortcodes: d/h/p/l/i/b/c/m/t/s/html/embed/av. Prefer semantic aliases such as methodName/sortBy over numeric method/orderBy.",
        "search(action="fulltext") supports parentId to scope results within a document subtree, and hasTags to filter by tag presence.",
        "Right after creating or editing content, full-text and tag search can lag behind writes because SiYuan indexing is eventually consistent; brief retries are expected in live tests.",
      ],
      "helpResources": [
        "siyuan://help/action/search/{action}",
        "siyuan://help/tool-overview",
        "siyuan://help/examples",
        "siyuan://help/ai-layout-guide",
      ],
      "requiresConfirmation": [
        "find_replace",
      ],
      "sharedTopics": [
        "ai-layout-guide",
      ],
      "tool": "search",
      "writeWorkflow": [
        "Confirm the user-authorized target and operation scope.",
        "Call the same action with validateOnly=true to obtain preflight.commitArgs.",
        "Read the returned preview (targets, changes, risk) and confirm it matches the intended change; if not, do not commit. preview="full" returns complete before/after text.",
        "Copy preflight.commitArgs unchanged as the next call arguments; do not edit requestId, hashes, or business fields.",
        "Read the target back or inspect the returned receipt before reporting success.",
      ],
    },
